# LEARNER C, LOCAL, THE ACCUMULATED FIXES ON ONE TOWN (Town01), because two do not fit on this machine.
# = slurm/local_frl_control_t05t01_ar8.env with ENV_TOWNS=Town01 and one env (no FRL_PARALLEL): the control
#   stream as the frozen trunk, action repeat 8, the slow-arrival rule, the expert rows of BOTH towns pinned,
#   30,000 IQL warm-up updates, 60,000 decisions -- every learner and reward setting is that overlay's.
# WHY ONE TOWN: the user asked for two ("finetune locally first - try two towns"), and the two-town overlay
# was tried first. Measured 2026-11-14 on the 12 GB RTX 4070: Town05's Epic server held 6.7 GB and Town01's
# 4.9 GB, 11.6 GB before the learner's first update, which then failed (CUBLAS_STATUS_ALLOC_FAILED in the
# IQL warm-up). CARLA 0.9.15 gives every server a 4000 MB texture pool (Config/DefaultEngine.ini,
# r.Streaming.PoolSize); making two fit means capping it, which changes the renderer's memory and has not
# been checked against the recorded frames, so it is not done here. Town01 is the town of the earlier
# local learner-C runs (user 2026-11-10: "lets train in town01").
# Scoring is unchanged: Town05 AND Town01 (slurm/il_eval_val_chw_jr_strict1m_ar8.env). The RL's own
# experience is Town01 only, so the Town05 column is transfer from Town01 plus the pinned Town05 expert rows.
. "$REPO/slurm/local_frl_control_t05t01_ar8.env"
export ENV_TOWNS=Town01
export FRL_PARALLEL=0
